WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:10.220
King's Knight, four brave warriors have set out into the kingdom of Isander to rescue Princess Claire from the grip of a fiendish dragon.

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:33.180
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.820
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.300
And I'm Joe. Guys, the algorithms are really trying to fool us now.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:46.500
They really wanted us to believe this was some kind of like RPG or maybe a puzzle platformer,

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:54.480
but instead it is once again a shmup, just like the adventures of Dino Ricky was a caveman shmup.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:59.720
This is now a choose your RPG character shmup.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:08.360
Never did I imagine that this game called King's Knight was going to be a multi-character story based level progression shmup.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:12.100
It's also the subcategory terraforming shmup.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:13.740
I'm sure we'll get into.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:19.440
Yeah. The famous category of terraforming in video games.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:28.080
Yeah. I think that Square, 1989 Square had been listening to the podcast and they know that we often have negative things to say about shmups.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.380
They're like, well, maybe we can pull a fast one on them.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.220
And this does kind of hit, you know, you mentioned Square there.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:40.460
This hits their notes of what they're about to do with Final Fantasy or what they've already done with Final Fantasy over in Japan.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:42.200
But we haven't gotten it yet.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:56.320
The point being that this does have a lot of familiar RPG tropes like your character leveling up or, you know, the kinds of characters you are, the quest that you're on to rescue the princess from a dragon.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.380
All the elements are there.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.180
It's just not an RPG at all, actually.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:16.520
Yeah. Like the tile set looks like if you look at a screenshot of this game and maybe there weren't any projectiles on the screen, I would have thought that this was just a standard four direction top down RPG.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:21.820
And maybe it's just like an RPG maker hack where they just made the screen scroll.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:27.460
And but no, it's the weirdest thing, the way it looks, the way it feels.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:35.300
Yeah. Even if there were projectiles on the screen, I mean, I would just think it was like an action RPG sort of thing or like a Legend of Zelda type style thing.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:40.300
It looks the screenshot really led me to believe, like, wow, this is going to be an awesome RPG experience.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:53.700
And I said multi character and I mean it because in this shmup you play as a knight, a wizard, a monster and a thief and individually like they're not like a party or anything until the very end of the game.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:03:03.700
You just kind of start with the knight, either complete his level or he dies, and then you just get the next screen with the wizard and then you do his whole thing.

00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:10.800
And, you know, each one just kind of is its own separate gameplay thing that's removed from one another.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:18.000
I think it's a really weird experience if you play this blind, like if you don't read the back of the box or you don't read the manual.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:29.720
The idea that you just press start are greeted with what you think is your character in a shmup as you're going to go like level to level similar to how every other shmup like Gradius has handled it.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:38.080
Instead, if you die or if you move on, it just then teleports you to the next character, to the next character, to the next character.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.700
It's almost like. And now for something entirely different.

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:43.200
Right. What is happening there?

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:49.620
And what did you guys think of that idea to have, you know, four different characters that you take control of?

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:55.660
On paper, I really like the concept of it, of the like, all right, you did your do.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:04:00.980
And, you know, failing doesn't fail the game at this point.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:05.880
Like it's wow. OK, maybe this game is harder than I thought.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:08.320
And you're not even expected to complete it.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:11.480
So, of course, you're going to move on to the next guy and see how you do with that guy.

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:16.880
And then later you find out that you you play as all the surviving characters.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:23.400
So, again, on paper and with that simple of a description of it, it's a pretty neat idea.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.160
Yeah, I kind of agree there.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.000
