Great. Now let's talk about that final level.

00:25:05.000 --> 00:25:20.460
All the characters coming together, you get a nice little screen that says, help the princess, and you see your four characters, and then they are arranged, basically, as, like, a compass, north, south, east, and west, and you're still only playing as one of them.

00:25:20.460 --> 00:25:31.080
But this was probably the opportunity to do something cool where, you know, like, you could actually, like, swap freely between the characters and stuff like that.

00:25:31.260 --> 00:25:39.940
However, they've decided to embrace the directional pads even more, and now you are forced to think about which direction you're going to change into.

00:25:40.120 --> 00:25:43.100
Not that it matters, really, because they're all just the same character.

00:25:43.100 --> 00:25:51.280
I guess, you know, if levels do matter, maybe you leveled up the monster better than the knight or something, and so you would want to have him as your frontrunner.

00:25:51.640 --> 00:25:56.700
The only other, like, noticeable change here is that, finally, we have a use for the B button.

00:25:56.940 --> 00:26:03.960
The whole game, the B button is obsolete, and the A button is just what you use to attack, and it's the only thing you can use to do anything.

00:26:04.160 --> 00:26:07.520
The B button finally comes into play, but I didn't care.

00:26:07.520 --> 00:26:09.260
Well, so, okay.

00:26:09.820 --> 00:26:21.800
So, when you start this final level, you're not just shown, like, if you did this game correctly, you're shown all four of your guys, and you're sort of arranged in that cross pattern.

